# Recorded fingerprints of the SUT migrations directories the seeder writes into
# (versola-loadgen-dev-spec.md §3.4). One line per directory: <path> <sha256>.
#
# The value is SHA-256 over `<filename>:<sha256(contents)>\n` for every .sql file in the
# directory, sorted by filename -- see versola.loadgen.seed.MigrationFingerprint for why the
# contents are hashed and not just the listing.
#
# If SutSchemaGuardSpec fails against these values, auth's or central's schema has moved.
# READ THE MIGRATION DIFF FIRST. The question to answer is not "what is the new hash" but
# "does versola.loadgen.seed.SutSchema still describe every column a seeded user needs, and
# does SeedRows still write a value for each of them". Re-record only after answering it.
#
# Which directories appear here is derived from SutSchema.fingerprintedMigrationDirectories,
# not chosen here: a seeded table in a service not listed below fails the guard until its
# directory is added. That is why edge is absent -- the seeder writes no edge table yet.

auth/implementations/postgres/migrations 831cff0b712169b8c8d6e1c5d8c3d8cfe741ab2053bfa27aea889f0e79377c1b
central/implementations/postgres/migrations 2fdcb3ab0a473a9e921f0fa2e5f8ea941fcf61fb68e1eb6e6f5caac985c96f22
